# File: server/.env.example
# Purpose: Server environment settings and local configuration defaults.
# Responsibility: Jed Manaloto, backend development.
#
# Implementation guide.
#
# Integration contract:
# Required: JWT_SECRET and CLIENT_ORIGIN. PORT and DB_PATH have documented local defaults.
# SEED_DEMO controls optional demo data, never a database reset.
#
# Acceptance criteria:
# A teammate can fill in their local .env without asking which values belong to the server.
#
# Implementation notes:
# All lines here are comments until you implement the template. Actual .env files must stay
# untracked.
#
# Implementation steps:
# 1. After reading this guide, write the actual example variable assignments using harmless
#    example values. Copy the completed template to server/.env for local use.
# 2. Document PORT with local default 4000, JWT_SECRET with an empty placeholder, DB_PATH with
#    local value ./data/app.db, and CLIENT_ORIGIN with http://localhost:5173.
# 3. Also document NODE_ENV, defaulting to development locally, and an optional SEED_DEMO
#    switch, defaulting to false. env.js is the only place that reads these values.
# 4. Generate a long random JWT secret locally. Set real production values in Render settings;
#    never include them in this template or in the client.
# 5. On Render use DB_PATH=/var/data/app.db only after mounting a persistent disk at
#    /var/data. Set CLIENT_ORIGIN to the exact Vercel production origin, without a path or
#    trailing slash.
# 6. Treat any Vercel preview origin as a separate deliberate allowlist decision. Do not
#    replace the CORS origin check with a wildcard to make previews work.
#
# Related files and dependencies:
# server/src/config/env.js
# server/src/app.js
# server/src/db/connection.js
